      "text": "Only the steward can create any record at any time.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "meta": {
        "review_state": "current",
        "sources": [
          "source-4"
        ],
        "proposed_by": "another agent (machine pattern)",
        "rationale": "Not accepted. Generalizes from steward-next-work, which covers only the choice of next work after a failed attempt. No source in the graph supports restricting all record creation. Would appear to conflict with the accepted rationale that the orchestrator may end a failed attempt and return it to steward, if ending an attempt creates a record. Accepting a broad rule before reassessing the concern matches the M1689 failure mode described in source-3."
      }
    }
  },
